Found along the way, not introduced by this PR: `parse()` returns `null` for modified function keys, while `matches()` accepts the same sequences. This already happens on 8.2 with ctrl:

```php
$parser->parse("\e[1;5P");               // null, but matches(..., 'ctrl+f1') is true
$parser->parse("\e[15;5~");              // null, but matches(..., 'ctrl+f5') is true
$parser->parse("\e[1;9P");               // null, but matches(..., 'super+f1') is true
```

`parseKittySequence()` only handles the `u` form, the arrow and Home/End letters, and `~` codes 2/3/5/6/7/8. It has no case for `CSI 1;<mods> P/Q/R/S` (F1–F4) or the `~` codes of F1–F12 (11–24). This should be fixed in a separate PR.

